{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterRankTwo","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterGeometricRepresentationFull","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.dihedralExact_le_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.dihedralExact_le_three","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L252-L310","doc":"**`s_i s_j` has order exactly `M i j` whenever `M i j ≤ 3`.**\n\nBoth cases come from `CoxeterGeometricRepresentationFull`'s unconditional cell faithfulness:\n`[i, j]` reduced at `M i j = 2` and `[i, j, i]` reduced at `M i j = 3`. If a smaller power were\ntrivial the corresponding word would collapse to something of length `≤ 1`.\n\n**Superseded as an input** by `CoxeterDihedralOrder.dihedralExact_full`, which proves the same\npredicate for every `M i j`. Kept because the argument is independent and elementary — no\ntrigonometry, no Chebyshev recursion — so it is a cheap cross-check on the general result at the\nonly bond orders type `A` ever uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.exists_reduced_alternating_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.exists_reduced_alternating_tail","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L200-L248","doc":"**The dihedral descent lemma.** If `i` and `j` are both right descents of `w`, then the bond\norder `M i j` is finite and positive, and `w` has a reduced word whose tail is the alternating\nblock of length `M i j` — in both spellings, with the same prefix. A single braid move at that tail\nmoves between them.\n\nThe `0 < M i j` conjunct is *derived*, not assumed: two distinct descents give `(σᵢσⱼ)^k = 1` for\n`k = ℓ(v) > 0`, and `CoxeterDihedralOrder.bond_ne_zero_of_pow_eq_one` refutes that at an infinite\nbond. It is returned rather than left to the caller because the caller needs it to split off the\ntail's last letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.alternatingWord_reduced_of_both_descents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.alternatingWord_reduced_of_both_descents","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L126-L196","doc":"**The rank-two core.** An element of `W_{i,j}` with both `i` and `j` as right descents is the\nproduct of **both** alternating words of length `M i j`, each of them reduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.exists_reducedWord_concat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.exists_reducedWord_concat","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L92-L124","doc":"A right descent is witnessed by a reduced `J`-word ending in that letter, when the element\nlies in `W_J`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.isRightDescent_of_minRep_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.isRightDescent_of_minRep_mul","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L72-L83","doc":"**Descents pass through the cut.** A right descent of `u · v` lying in `J` is a right descent\nof `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.length_minRep_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralDescent.length_minRep_mul","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralDescent.lean#L64-L70","doc":"`ℓ(u · v) = ℓ(u) + ℓ(v)` for `u` a minimal coset representative and `v ∈ W_J`. The element\nform of `length_minRep_mul_wordProd'`, obtained by choosing an ambient-reduced `J`-word for `v`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}